## What this software does

Roadcast performs read-only observation of memory in a process running on the
user's own vehicle head unit. It does not write vehicle properties, does not
write into any other process, does not transmit CAN frames, does not invoke
vehicle controls, and does not alter ECU state. These constraints are
structural project invariants, not configuration. See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md.

Roadcast does not circumvent any technological protection measure and contains
no rooting, unlocking, or exploit mechanism. It requires a head unit that
already grants the necessary access.

